Start the Eshu MCP server

Usage:
  eshu mcp start [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help                    help for start
      --host string             Host to bind HTTP MCP server (default "0.0.0.0")
  -p, --port int                Port for HTTP MCP server (default 8080)
      --profile string          Runtime profile for a new local owner: local_authoritative (default; embedded NornicDB graph for call-graph and Cypher answers) or local_lightweight (Postgres only, no graph). For a Neo4j-backed authoritative owner, set ESHU_QUERY_PROFILE and ESHU_GRAPH_BACKEND instead.
  -t, --transport string        Transport mode: stdio, http, or sse (default "stdio")
      --workspace-root string   Explicit workspace root for the local Eshu owner

Global Flags:
      --database string   Temporarily override database backend
  -V, --visual            Show results as interactive graph visualization
